                        {'body': 'For the normal quadric cone $A=k[x,y,z]/(xy-z^2)$, the height-one prime $(x,z)$ defines a divisor class that '
                                 'detects failure of unique factorization.  It is the standard model where divisor class groups distinguish '
                                 'normality from factoriality.',
                         'title': 'A nontrivial class on a quadric cone'},
